{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"From Breda I continued on by diligence at 10 o’clock in the morning, for three run daily from Antwerp to Amsterdam, all via The Hague, and likewise three in return; — from Brussels to Paris, diligences also run every day, one is in Paris in 36 hours for 25 francs, what a temptation! had it not been so late in the season, and besides — had I had news from you, — could one have resisted such a temptation? Likewise in Rotterdam, here a steamboat goes once a week to London — punctual and infallible, unless there is very bad storm — in 24 hours. But now from Breda it went on yesterday without a break, — fertile land, but entirely now on brick-paved roads, like the sidewalk in Berlin — to Mordyk, from there by steamboat across a bay of the sea, the Holland Diep, 1/2 hour wide — my dear friend, the southwest, which had brought me such fine weather for so long, also helped with the better crossing; here ships came from afar, a proud three-masted ship, like a Sultan: majestic white turban, equally swollen white middle garment, then a white, wider lower garment, and a cloak behind, as the figure shows?). From here to Dordrecht, — large seaport, forty, or God knows how many thousand inhabitants; — from here in true Holland, — all houses of reddish bricks, with white lines as if made with a ruler, no edge, no corner crumbled or blunted, — beautiful canals, planted with trees, running through the city, everything full of large ships, the straight beautiful quays everywhere; — then again after 3 o’clock across the wide Meuse; then at 5 o’clock in Rotterdam; what a large city again! then through Delft and after half an hour into beautiful The Hague. The Hague is in fact a village — everywhere beautiful green meadows, so from Dordrecht on! The cleanest vegetable gardens, as nicely kept as Mrs. Voß can keep them, interrupted by rows of trees and cut off from the highway, next to which a canal always runs, and from each other, — cattle everywhere on them, — all black- and white-spotted, they also stay on the meadow at night, one sees people in the evening milking the cows; one travels among all the Potters and Berghems. — This morning out of the gate into a forest, like the Berlin Zoo, only more beautiful alleys of beeches and oaks, no undergrowth — all high and leafy forest; — one hour to Scheveningen, here I saw the unbounded North Sea, the German Sea — my friend the southwest blew strongly and brought the most beautiful waves. — Then I saw the gallery, afternoon strolled in the beautiful woods, more beautiful than the Aue near Cassel, splendid water pieces like in Charlottenburg; — then also once a French comedy and indeed three in one evening seen; I had to rest, for I have walked and stood a lot; — in the gallery is a Württemberg inspector, — beautiful, very beautiful things. — I have today before the mirror tied my neckerchief and seen that I, as I believe, have become thinner, for I have had many fatigues, — but I am otherwise healthy and vigorous and well; also with the money it is still going well, — I have lost, I believe, also nothing yet, and I am almost annoyed about it, for in something one must have bad luck, — but I calculate that I pay for everything in that I have no letters from you"}}],"created":1795218975,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":773,"prompt_tokens":919,"total_tokens":1692,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-3unRPLZ3FvgGLXfxENyIuhpch4CHySKg","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":919,"prompt_ms":959.798,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0443939064200218,"prompt_per_second":957.4931391813693,"predicted_n":773,"predicted_ms":18253.2,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.644041450777202,"predicted_per_second":42.29395393684395}}